            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kristie Goble"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I thought these were just great! This is our new sugar cookie and basic cookie batter to play with! I added lemon zest and juice and they were delish! We used multi color sugar and they were so pretty! They looked like a bakery cookie. I used a melon ball scoop and flatten with a mason jar bottom. Perfect size cookie!",
            "datePublished": "2014-08-16T09:58:30.107Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "mimi"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made these for the kids today. I substituted the white sugar for brown as it was all I had on hand.\nAfter I rolled the dough into balls, I dipped the tops with candy rounds. I missed the step to press them down with a glass but they turned out awesome anyway. Kids love them!",
            "datePublished": "2014-10-26T13:15:38.597Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Shelley"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Our new favorite cookie. I am making these instead of sugar cookies this year. They are great the way they are. Or dust with powdered sugar. Dip in white chocolate. Fill with walnuts. Or frost. They would look cute decorated as Christmas ornaments. I traded 1/4 cup sugar for 1/4 cup measurable stevia. Next time, I will try 1/2 and 1/2. Love 'em.",
            "datePublished": "2010-12-17T08:37:13.813Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Lorrie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Super easy to make for a beginner baker, with ingredients you already have in the house. I loved that they were sweet enough to satisfy a sugar craving, but not so sweet it taste like it will make you sick. A great way to make something just to have around the house for the occasional snacker. I didn’t have a full cup of butter, so I did have to use A quarter cup of pumpkin to make up the difference. The pumpkin did not change the overall taste of the cookie and was a good substitute for the better. I only had to cook it for 10 minutes, because I prefer a chewier cookie.",
            "datePublished": "2023-11-26T02:56:58.108Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "VMAX"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I added 1/2 cup of Chai tea mix to enhance the flavor. They turned out very good. A very simple tasty recipe!",
            "datePublished": "2011-02-26T19:04:56.490Z"
          },
          {
